        "description": "After three PlayStation generations of waiting, Grand Theft Auto 6 is finally here. And while it\u2019s advertised that it plays best on PlayStation, is that actually the case? In this video we\u2019re going to look at the graphical differences between the game running on a base PlayStation 5 vs a PlayStation 5 pro. \n \nOn the base PlayStation 5 you\u2019re going to get the game outputting at an upscaled 4K resolution from an internal 1440p that runs at a solid 30 fps. The upscaling is a bit softer on the base PS5 due to it not using PSSR like the PS5 Pro, but that\u2019s not to say the game is blurry or anything. There are also some instances where the frame rate can drop to a sub-20fps, but that\u2019s few and far in-between. The base PS5 does feature Ray Tracing, but it\u2019s not as robust as the more expensive Pro will get you. \n \nSpeaking of the PS5 Pro. If you\u2019re using Sony's flagship box you will also get an upscaled 4K resolution that is a little sharper thanks to PSSR, but it\u2019s still pulling from an inter",
